WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.633
Reranking with cross-encoders.

2
00:00:02.933 --> 00:00:07.332
Six lines of code, often a ten to twenty five point jump in hit-rate.

3
00:00:07.332 --> 00:00:08.033
Here's how.

4
00:00:09.233 --> 00:00:10.800
The trick is two stages.

5
00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:14.500
First, retrieve generously and cheaply, built for recall.

6
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:18.033
Then rescore a small set carefully, built for precision.

7
00:00:19.233 --> 00:00:20.400
Two kinds of model.

8
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:26.667
A bi-encoder embeds the query and each document separately, so the two texts never see each other.

9
00:00:26.967 --> 00:00:30.500
A cross-encoder reads them together through a full transformer.

10
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:35.467
That makes it far more accurate, but far too slow to run against a million chunks.

11
00:00:35.767 --> 00:00:38.867
So narrow with the fast one, decide with the accurate one.

12
00:00:40.067 --> 00:00:41.067
Here's the funnel.

13
00:00:41.367 --> 00:00:43.500
The whole index holds millions of chunks.

14
00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:46.800
The fast retriever returns a generous top fifty.

15
00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:50.200
The cross-encoder rescores those fifty precisely.

16
00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:52.733
And only the top five go into the prompt.

17
00:00:53.933 --> 00:00:54.900
Here's the code.

18
00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:57.300
Stage one pulls fifty candidates.

19
00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:01.100
The cross-encoder scores each query and chunk pair together.

20
00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:03.533
We sort by score and keep the top five.

21
00:01:04.733 --> 00:01:05.700
Now measure it.

22
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:11.067
On a twenty question eval, hit-rate at five went from sixty percent to eighty five.

23
00:01:11.367 --> 00:01:14.367
Nothing else tried that week came close, per line of code.

24
00:01:15.567 --> 00:01:16.867
Here is why it works.

25
00:01:17.167 --> 00:01:19.567
A user asks why the March burn aborted.

26
00:01:19.867 --> 00:01:28.767
The log says TLI maneuver terminated, with no shared words, so the bi-encoder ranked it twenty seventh, invisible to a top five prompt.

27
00:01:29.067 --> 00:01:32.833
The cross-encoder reads both together, and moves it to rank one.

28
00:01:34.033 --> 00:01:34.892
Let's recap.

29
00:01:34.892 --> 00:01:36.967
Bi-encoders give fast recall.

30
00:01:37.267 --> 00:01:39.500
Cross-encoders give precise ranking.

31
00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:42.067
Retrieve fifty, rescore, keep five.

32
00:01:42.367 --> 00:01:44.883
And measure hit-rate before and after.

33
00:01:44.883 --> 00:01:47.200
Next up: retrieval pipeline design.
